description: CommonMark reference-style link `[text][label]` — the link text is the body, the second bracket pair holds the LABEL that resolves to a `[label]: target` definition via the per-parser ref store (populated by the `markdown-ref-def` block rule). Targets get the same TW-md-plugin treatment as inline LINK: `#` prefix forces internal-tiddler routing, `<...>` wraps allow spaces in tiddler titles, the def's `"title"` becomes the rendered `tooltip`. Definitions must appear BEFORE their usage in the source — this is single-pass (no pre-scan); unresolved labels render as literal `[text][label]`.
